Keith Hearn brought the following to the attention of
rec.games.roguelike.nethack:
> Pet arch-lichs are pretty dangerous if you don't have MR.
[...]
> You can't just lock it in a isolated room because it teleports back to
> you. You really don't want to leave it on another level while you
> transact your business, because it will become less tame. And since it
> doesn't eat, you have no way to increase its tameness, so sooner or
> later you'll come back and find it's not your pet anymore.

So leave it in a dungeon branch you don't plan on visiting again.
Sokoban's best for this, as even if you do forget and wander back in
after the lich goes wild, you only have to hit it until it flees to the
other stairs, allowing you to escape.


